##
   Methods executing in the VM, which AGENTS.md 2.10 requires of every construct.

   The `$` on each `impl` member is the whole point of this fixture. Without it
   a method is emitted as a plain `Counter_get` with no dollar marker, and every
   attempt to call it from a dollar scope fails with "Cannot call a non dollar
   function" -- so the entire method feature was unreachable in the VM even
   though the byte-identical hand-written `$ func Counter_get(self: Counter)`
   worked fine. The `impl` parser did not accept qualifiers on its members; it
   now does, the same way a top-level `func` does.

   Note the receiver is still an ordinary parameter and `marked` still applies to
   field access through a reference -- `$` changes who may call a function, not
   what the function may do.
##
contract HasGet { func get(): i32 }

struct Counter: HasGet { n: i32 }

impl Counter {
  $ func get(self: Counter): i32 { return self.n; }
  $ func scaled(self: Counter, k: i32): i32 { return self.n * k; }
}

$ func compute(): i32 {
  var c: mut Counter = .Counter{.n = 3i32};
  return c.get() + c.scaled(4i32);
}

expose func run(): i32 { return compute(); }

$ func foo(): u32 {
  var a = $${ compute() };
  return 0u32;
}
